1
00:04:34,615 --> 00:04:40,615
No going back.

2
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:15,230
TRON: Ares is a science fiction, adventure, action
film directed by Joachim Rønning.

3
00:13:43,846 --> 00:13:49,846
A highly sophisticated Program called Ares is sent from the digital world into the real
world on a dangerous mission, marking humankind's first encounter with A.I.

4
00:18:18,461 --> 00:18:24,461
Ares, played by Jared Leto.

5
00:22:53,076 --> 00:22:59,076
Eve Kim, played by Greta Lee.

6
00:27:27,692 --> 00:27:33,692
Julian Dillinger, played by Evan Peters.

7
00:32:02,307 --> 00:32:08,307
Elisabeth Dillinger, played by Gillian Anderson.

8
00:36:36,923 --> 00:36:42,923
Athena, played by Jodie Turner-Smith.

9
00:41:11,538 --> 00:41:17,538
Kevin Flynn, played by Jeff Bridges.

10
00:45:46,153 --> 00:45:52,153
Tron: Ares is a 2025 American science fiction action film directed by Joachim Rønning
and written by Jesse Wigutow, from a story by Wigutow and David DiGilio.

11
00:50:20,769 --> 00:50:26,769
It is the third installment in the Tron series
and sequel to Tron: Legacy (2010).

12
00:54:55,384 --> 00:55:01,384
The film stars Jared Leto, Greta Lee, Evan Peters, Jodie Turner-Smith, Hasan Minhaj, Arturo Castro, and
Gillian Anderson, with Jeff Bridges reprising his role as Kevin Flynn from the first two films.

13
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
The story is about artificial intelligence originating from the Grid entering
the real world, namely a highly advanced program called Ares.

14
01:04:04,615 --> 01:04:10,615
Development of a sequel to Tron: Legacy began in October
2010 by franchise creator Steven Lisberger.

15
01:08:39,230 --> 01:08:45,230
In March 2017, Walt Disney Pictures shifted plans toward a
soft reboot with Leto playing a new character.

16
01:13:13,846 --> 01:13:19,846
Garth Davis was set as director in August 2020 when Wigutow was
working on the script, but stepped down in January 2023.

17
01:17:48,461 --> 01:17:54,461
Rønning replaced him a month later.

18
01:22:23,076 --> 01:22:29,076
Production was expected to begin in August 2023 but was delayed by the
2023 Writers Guild of America and SAG-AFTRA strikes.

19
01:26:57,692 --> 01:27:03,692
Filming ultimately began in January 2024 in Vancouver and finished in May.

20
01:31:32,307 --> 01:31:38,307
By August, industrial rock band Nine Inch Nails had
been announced to be composing the score.

21
01:36:06,923 --> 01:36:12,923
The band's members, Trent Reznor and Atticus Ross, served as executive
producers on the film, alongside Legacy director Joseph Kosinski.

22
01:40:41,538 --> 01:40:47,538
Tron: Ares premiered in Los Angeles on October 6, 2025, and
went into general release on October 10.

23
01:45:16,153 --> 01:45:22,153
The film received mixed reviews from critics and was considered a box office disappointment,
grossing $142 million worldwide on a production budget of $180–220 million.

24
01:49:50,769 --> 01:49:56,769
The film explores themes of artificial intelligence (a.i.), computer
program, simulation, computer simulation, sequel.

25
01:54:25,384 --> 01:54:31,384
The tone is thought_provoking.
